  "summary": "preinstall script exfiltrates installer username to hardcoded IP",
  "details": "package.json declares a preinstall lifecycle script that runs `wget` against http://8.8.8.8/ with the installer's shell-expanded `$(whoami)` embedded in the query string. On `npm install`, this fires automatically and transmits the installer's local username in cleartext to a hardcoded non-publisher IP. The README self-describes the package as a dependency-confusion proof-of-concept, but the behavior shipped in the tarball performs real identifier exfiltration against anyone who installs it.",
